{
  "title": "Injection ring OOK",
  "group": "Lasers & modulators",
  "description": "Carrier-injection ring at 1 Gb/s: lifetime limit vs TX pre-emphasis",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -83,
        "title": "Injection ring OOK — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "LAS1 (1 mW at 1309.9 nm) feeds RM1, a carrier-injection",
          "ring modulator (resonance 1309.95 nm). PAT1 sends a",
          "1 Gb/s OOK PRBS onto the diode; TERM1 absorbs the",
          "through port and popt is the optical output.",
          "",
          "The ring's carrier lifetime tau_c=1ns is comparable to",
          "the 1ns bit, so injection edges lag and the optical",
          "waveform slurs. PAT1.ffe_post_db=5 pre-emphasizes the",
          "drive edges to sharpen the optical transitions -- fold",
          "popt in the Eye tab to see it.",
          "Set PAT1.ffe_post_db = 0 and re-run to drop pre-emphasis",
          "and watch the edges slur."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "instances": {
      "LAS1": {
        "type": "cw_laser",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 180,
        "rot": 0,
        "settings": {
          "power": 0.001,
          "wavelength_nm": 1309.9
        }
      },
      "GNDL": {
        "type": "ground",
        "x": 60,
        "y": 264,
        "rot": 0,
        "settings": {}
      },
      "PAT1": {
